    <h3>1. What Are Cookies?</h3>
    <p>Cookies are small text files that websites may store on a user's device.</p>
    <p>They help websites remember information about a session, maintain certain functions, and understand how users interact with pages.</p>
    <p>StudyShare may also use similar technologies where necessary.</p>

    <h3>2. Why StudyShare Uses Cookies</h3>
    <p>Cookies and similar technologies may be used for the following purposes.</p>

    <h4>A. Essential Functionality</h4>
    <p>These technologies may support:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>User authentication.</li>
      <li>Session management.</li>
      <li>Security-related functions.</li>
      <li>Maintaining the continuity of website interactions.</li>
      <li>Security-related functionality.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some of these technologies are necessary for the website to operate correctly.</p>

    <h4>B. Analytics</h4>
    <p>Where Google Analytics is enabled, analytics technologies may be used to understand:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>How many users visit the website.</li>
      <li>Which pages are viewed.</li>
      <li>How users navigate through the platform.</li>
      <li>Which traffic sources bring visitors to the website.</li>
      <li>How website performance and engagement change over time.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Analytics information is used to understand and improve the user experience.</p>

    <h4>C. Preferences</h4>
    <p>If preference-related features are implemented, cookies or similar technologies may help remember relevant settings.</p>

    <h3>3. Google Analytics</h3>
    <p>StudyShare may use Google Analytics to measure website traffic and user interactions.</p>
    <p>When enabled, Google Analytics may collect information such as page views, interactions, browser details, and information about how users arrive at the website.</p>
    <p>Google Analytics may use cookies or similar technologies to provide these measurements.</p>
    <p>For additional information, please review Google's privacy documentation and the Google Analytics terms applicable to the service.</p>

    <h3>4. First-Party and Third-Party Cookies</h3>
    <p>First-party cookies are set by the website you are visiting.</p>
    <p>Third-party cookies or similar technologies may be associated with external services integrated into the website.</p>
    <p>The availability and behavior of these technologies depend on the services enabled and the website's current configuration.</p>

    <h3>5. Session Cookies</h3>
    <p>StudyShare may use session-related cookies to maintain authenticated sessions and support protected features.</p>
    <p>Some cookies may expire when the session ends, while others may remain for a configured period.</p>
    <p>The actual duration depends on the relevant cookie and session configuration.</p>

    <h3>6. Managing Cookies</h3>
    <p>You can manage or delete cookies through your browser settings.</p>
    <p>Depending on your browser, you may be able to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Block cookies.</li>
      <li>Delete stored cookies.</li>
      <li>Restrict third-party cookies.</li>
      <li>Receive notifications when cookies are stored.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Blocking essential cookies may prevent some StudyShare features, such as authentication, from functioning correctly.</p>

    <h3>7. Consent and Cookie Preferences</h3>
    <p>Where consent is required by applicable law, StudyShare should provide appropriate consent and preference mechanisms before activating technologies that require consent.</p>
    <p>The availability of these controls depends on the website's implemented configuration.</p>

    <h3>8. Changes to This Cookie Policy</h3>
